  "prompt": "[system]\n\n    You generate compact, robust Python TSP metaheuristics.\n    You must follow the requested interface exactly, always preserve tour validity.\n    \n\n[user]\nPARENTS:\nCandidate cand_000021: rand_ils_sa_restart\n\nStatus: valid; distance: 7.81975\n\nThought: Random-start nearest neighbor construction, then 2-opt local search, then iterated local search with double-bridge perturbation and simulated annealing acceptance (cooling temperature), and multiple restarts (5 runs) to improve exploration. Increased SA iterations to 30 for deeper search within time budget.\n\nCode:\n\n```python\n\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef solve_tsp(distance_matrix: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    n = len(distance_matrix)\n    best_tour = None\n    best_dist = np.inf\n\n    def two_opt(tour):\n        improved = True\n        while improved:\n            improved = False\n            for i in range(n - 2):\n                for j in range(i + 2, n):\n                    a, b = tour[i], tour[(i+1) % n]\n                    c, d = tour[j], tour[(j+1) % n]\n                    delta = (distance_matrix[a, c] + distance_matrix[b, d] - distance_matrix[a, b] - distance_matrix[c, d])\n                    if delta < -1e-12:\n                        tour[i+1:j+1] = np.flip(tour[i+1:j+1])\n                        improved = True\n                        break\n                if improved:\n                    break\n        return tour\n\n    def double_bridge(tour):\n        arr = tour.copy()\n        i, j, k, l = np.random.randint(0, n, 4)\n        a, b, c, d = sorted([i, j, k, l])\n        seg1 = arr[a:b]\n        seg2 = arr[b:c]\n        seg3 = arr[c:d]\n        seg4 = np.concatenate([arr[d:], arr[:a]])\n        return np.concatenate([seg1, seg4, seg3, seg2])\n\n    for restart in range(5):\n        # Random-start nearest neighbor\n        start = np.random.randint(n)\n        tour = [start]\n        unvisited = set(range(n))\n        unvisited.remove(start)\n        while unvisited:\n            last = tour[-1]\n            nearest = min(unvisited, key=lambda x: distance_matrix[last, x])\n            tour.append(nearest)\n            unvisited.remove(nearest)\n        tour = np.array(tour, dtype=np.int32)\n        tour = two_opt(tour)\n        current_dist = np.sum(distance_matrix[tour[:-1], tour[1:]]) + distance_matrix[tour[-1], tour[0]]\n        if current_dist < best_dist - 1e-12:\n            best_dist = current_dist\n            best_tour = tour.copy()\n            report_best_tour(best_tour)\n\n        # Simulated annealing schedule\n        T0 = 0.1 * np.max(distance_matrix)\n        T = T0\n        num_iters = 30\n\n        for iteration in range(num_iters):\n            perturbed = double_bridge(tour)\n            new_tour = two_opt(perturbed)\n            new_dist = np.sum(distance_matrix[new_tour[:-1], new_tour[1:]]) + distance_matrix[new_tour[-1], new_tour[0]]\n            delta = new_dist - current_dist\n            if delta < -1e-12 or np.random.random() < np.exp(-delta / T):\n                tour = new_tour\n                current_dist = new_dist\n                if current_dist < best_dist - 1e-12:\n                    best_dist = current_dist\n                    best_tour = tour.copy()\n                    report_best_tour(best_tour)\n            T = T0 * (1 - (iteration + 1) / num_iters)\n\n    # Final 2-opt on best tour\n    best_tour = two_opt(best_tour.copy())\n    best_dist = np.sum(distance_matrix[best_tour[:-1], best_tour[1:]]) + distance_matrix[best_tour[-1], best_tour[0]]\n    report_best_tour(best_tour)\n    return best_tour\n\n```\n\nVERBAL GRADIENT: follow the reflection below as the primary source of change.\n\nUse the supplied parents as supporting evidence only.\n\nPARENT-SPECIFIC LLM REFLECTIONS:\n\nParent cand_000021 LLM reflection:\n- Summary: Candidate improved tour length by 0.9% over best parent but increased mean runtime from 4.9s to 22.6s, still under 30s timeout.\n- Aim: Further reduce tour length by increasing restarts while keeping runtime under 28s through parameter balancing.\n- Preserve: two_opt local search; SA acceptance with cooling; double_bridge perturbation; report_best_tour usage\n- Change: Increase restarts from 5 to 6 and reduce SA iterations per restart from 30 to 25\n- Avoid: Exceeding 30s timeout on any instance; Removing valid permutation guarantee; Changing perturbation that yields invalid tours\n\nDistance is the search objective for TSP; lower distance is better.\n\nImplement a complete TSP metaheuristic inside this required entrypoint:\n\ndef solve_tsp(distance_matrix: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n\nRequirements:\n- Instances are symmetric Euclidean 2D-style TSPs represented by a distance matrix.\n- Minimize total TSP tour distance.\n- Return a 1D np.ndarray containing each node exactly once.\n- Do not repeat the start node at the end.\n- Always return a valid tour.\n- Use only distance_matrix; coordinates are not provided, but metric/geometric structure can be inferred from distances.\n- Create a valid tour early.\n- Call report_best_tour(tour) whenever a new best valid tour is found, assume this func already exists.\n- Do not use files, network, subprocesses, or external solvers.\n- Keep the code compact and robust.\n\ncorrect signature, valid tour on every return path,\nearly report_best_tour, allowed imports only, no I/O/network/subprocesses.\n\nReturn one JSON object and nothing else:\n\n{\n  \"name\": \"short_snake_case_name\",\n  \"thought\": \"high-level summary of the construction, improvement, and tie-break logic\",\n  \"code\": \"complete Python code as a JSON string\"\n}\nNo Markdown, fences, or text outside JSON. The code string must define solve_tsp.",
